        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-1197_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-1197_47435_lbl" />
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-04_47225_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important">Cash management program with Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-08_47226_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit">The following are the intermediary companies in the chain of ownership between Energy Transfer LP (DE) and Energy Transfer GC NGL Assets GP LLC (DE):</span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></p><p class="_Normal_"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit">Energy Transfer LP owns</span><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"> 1% GP interest in Energy Transfer GC NGL Pipelines LP through its </span><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important">100% of Energy Transfer GC NGL Assets GP LLC.</span></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-124_47227_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit">The following are the intermediary companies in the chain of ownership between Energy Transfer LP (DE) and Energy Transfer GC NGLs LLC (DE):</span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></p><p class="_Normal_"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none">Energy Transfer LP owns 99.0% LP interests in </span><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-decoration: none; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"><span> </span></span><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-decoration: none; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt">Energy Transfer GC NGL Pipelines LP through its </span><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-decoration: none; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important">100% ownership of Energy Transfer GC NGLs LLC.</span></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-295_47249_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>Schedule Page 114 Line No.: 1 Column: c</b></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $33.5 million are included in Account(s) 600.</span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-304_47232_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">Effective July 31, 2024, through a series of transactions Energy Transfer GC NGL Pipelines LP conveyed its 100% membership interest in Energy Transfer GC NGL Product Services LLC to Energy Transfer GC NGLs LLC, an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-335_47233_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">Cash management program with Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1197_47435_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)">Schedule Page 700 Line No.: 9 Column: b</b></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit">In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $3,400,000 are included in line 10, interstate operating revenue. These revenues represent a one-time event and are not representative of future revenues. </span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important">The cost of service results were calculated using the Cost of Service Model. This model calculates cost of service using the Trended Original Cost methodology promulgated by the FERC in Opinion No. 154-B, 31 FERC 61,377 (1985), as modified and clarified by subsequent rulings.</span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"><br /></span></p></div></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>